WEBVTT

00:10.850 --> 00:15.613
As our trajectory continues, the massive body

00:15.673 --> 00:18.836
of the parent planet moves directly between us

00:19.116 --> 00:19.776
and the sun.

00:23.119 --> 00:27.942
We are now entering the penumbra, the outer edge

00:28.002 --> 00:32.445
of the celestial shadow. The temperature will

00:32.485 --> 00:36.168
begin to drop rapidly as the light is obscured.

00:39.090 --> 00:43.498
Solar efficiency will fall to critical levels.

00:45.279 --> 00:49.762
Prepare for deep space isolation as we cross the

00:49.842 --> 00:50.482
threshold

00:53.424 --> 00:55.185
into total darkness.

01:24.904 --> 01:28.467
The edge of the planet is cutting the light

01:32.311 --> 01:36.335
A massive eclipse in the middle of the night

01:39.818 --> 01:43.399
Temperature drops on the console screen The

01:43.499 --> 01:47.700
coldest shadow that I've ever seen The solar

01:47.900 --> 01:52.641
rays are starting to freeze A sudden drop by a

01:52.741 --> 01:56.842
hundred degrees Entering the shadow, crossing

01:56.902 --> 02:02.423
the line Losing the light, losing the sign Power

02:02.563 --> 02:06.384
is draining, the cabin is dark Waiting in the

02:06.504 --> 02:11.606
black for a single spark Caught in the penumbra,

02:11.806 --> 02:16.147
cold and blind Leaving the warmth of the sun

02:16.167 --> 02:20.208
behind A temporary death in the deep space

02:20.288 --> 02:23.869
breeze Drifting completely on the dark space

02:23.969 --> 02:29.910
breeze Hold your breath, and wait for the dawn

02:31.330 --> 02:37.292
Caught in the penumbra, until the night is gone

02:43.755 --> 02:48.219
The machinery hums with a desperate sound A

02:48.340 --> 02:52.043
million miles from the solid ground The silence

02:52.203 --> 02:56.387
out here has a sharper edge Like standing alone

02:56.588 --> 03:01.331
on an icy ledge I close my eyes in the pitch black

03:01.451 --> 03:05.713
room Swallowed alive by the planetary tomb

03:06.193 --> 03:10.395
Entering the shadow, crossing the line Losing

03:10.435 --> 03:14.376
the light, losing the sign The power is

03:14.516 --> 03:18.558
draining, the cabin is dark Waiting in the black

03:18.658 --> 03:23.941
for a single spark Caught in the penumbra Cold

03:24.141 --> 03:28.583
and blind Leaving the warmth of the sun behind A

03:28.764 --> 03:32.486
temporary death in the deep space breeze

03:32.886 --> 03:36.148
Drifting completely on the dark space breeze

03:36.368 --> 03:44.112
Hold your breath And wait for the dawn Caught in

03:44.172 --> 03:48.875
the penumbra Until the night is gone

04:18.363 --> 04:23.028
Just a phase of the orbit. Just a test of the

04:23.108 --> 04:30.956
steel. The shadow is heavy. But the math is real.

04:33.518 --> 04:34.759
Wait for the transit.

04:37.202 --> 04:42.912
Wait for the light. Caught in the penumbra Cold

04:43.092 --> 04:47.493
and blind Leaving the warmth of the sun behind A

04:47.693 --> 04:51.393
temporary death in the deep space freeze

04:51.814 --> 04:55.054
Drifting completely on the dark space freeze

04:55.294 --> 05:02.996
Hold your breath And wait for the dawn Caught in

05:03.076 --> 05:07.777
the penumbra Until the night is gone

05:13.600 --> 05:15.002
Wait for the dawn

05:18.207 --> 05:22.453
The solar rays are dark In the penumbra

